# Stack skills must be used (not only installed)

Marketplace packs live under **`dev-agent/.agents/skills/`** (gitignored). They are useless unless the agent **Reads** them.

## Before implementing product code for a slug

1. `bash scripts/verify_stack_skills.sh <slug>`  
   - On `STACK_SKILLS_FAIL`: `bash scripts/verify_stack_skills.sh <slug> --install`
2. Open `projects/<slug>/factory/stack-skills.manifest`
3. **Read** every `SKILL.md` path listed (absolute paths under `.agents/skills/` and optional `projects/<slug>/.cursor/skills/`)
4. Follow those skills for the matching stack (ASP.NET, Angular/Ionic, MSSQL SPs, Supabase, …)

## Forbidden

- Implementing .NET / Angular / Ionic / SQL / Supabase behaviour while ignoring the manifest
- Vendoring packs into the **app** repo
- Assuming packs are in context without Reading the files (Cursor may not auto-load `.agents/skills` when the workspace root is the app)

## Factory skills vs stack skills

| Kind | Path | Auto-loaded when workspace is `dev-agent` |
|------|------|---------------------------------------------|
| Factory (`dev-*`) | `.cursor/skills/dev-*` | Yes |
| Stack packs | `.agents/skills/*` | **Not reliable** — use manifest + Read |
| Project overrides | `projects/<slug>/.cursor/skills/` | Read via manifest |
